WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:04.680
- [Narrator] $10 billion, then
47 billion, then 100 billion.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.540
The Adani Group's seven listed companies

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.180
have plummeted in market
value after a report

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.370
from short seller
Hindenburg Research accused

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.280
the conglomerate of wide ranging fraud.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.830
The Adani Group, headed by
billionaire Gautam Adani,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.413
said The report is full
of baseless allegations.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.920
Ben Foldy covers financial
and business issues

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:23.880
for The Wall Street Journal

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.630
and explains what you need to know.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.430
- The Adani Group is a
collection of companies.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.710
They run ports, they run airports,

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.880
they run coal-powered power
plants, they run coal terminals.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.920
Basically all the things
that you kind of need

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.010
to build a fast growing,
developing economy like India,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.230
and Hindenburg Research looks
for companies that they allege

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.300
are frauds or have accounting issues,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.610
and they then bet against the stock,

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.080
and then they publish the research

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.100
showing their allegations,
hoping that it will go down.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.750
They were largely responsible

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.100
for almost everything that happened

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.540
with a company called Nikola,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.550
which led to the founder being indicted

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.920
on fraud charges and convicted last year

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.060
in one of the biggest cases of
that type in recent history.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.530
Hindenburg's allegations about Adani

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.060
are largely around a network

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.130
of offshore companies that they allege

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.230
are tied to the Adani family

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.520
or their associates that they
use to manipulate the stock.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.680
- The report is a malicious combination

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.130
of selective misinformation,
stale, baseless

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.310
and discredited allegations
that have been tested

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.860
and rejected by India's highest codes.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.410
- Adani responded with a 413-page report.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.930
What was interesting about
the response is that it opened

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.990
on this note of Indian
nationalism, which really kind

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.660
of points to a defense
strategy for the company

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.730
but also, it points to
the company's identity

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:46.080
as being part and parcel
of the Indian growth story.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.613
- The fundamentals of our
company are very strong.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:57.009
Our balance sheet is
healthy and assets robust.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.460
We will continue to focus

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.090
on a long-term value creation and growth.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.837
- Adani has already suffered quite a bit.

00:02:07.837 --> 00:02:10.500
$100 billion in market cap
is nothing to sneeze at.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.240
To have something move
the market this much

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.406
within a couple days is pretty remarkable.

00:02:14.406 --> 00:02:17.073
(pensive music)

